ARCHITECTURE / APPROACH (ADR-002/004/005/006/011/013/014/015)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Stateless MaintenancePageContent rendered inside the shared PageContainer chrome; stateful MaintenancePage binds the
  view-model and collects itemsState/recordsState/displayPrefs/filter via collectAsStateWithLifecycle (ADR-002).
- The two feeds are projected onto the lifecycle-aware UiState surface (BaseFeedViewModel.asUiState), scoped to the
  global active vehicle (SelectedVehicleStore) exactly as the web queries are `enabled: vehicleId !== null`. Each panel
  renders its own loading/empty/error/content surface, so no section is ever hidden (ADR-011).
- All decode/derivation logic is framework-free in MaintenancePageModel.kt (off-device-testable Kotlin). The composable
  is a thin render layer; values fold through MaintenanceDisplayPrefs at the display boundary only.
- Design tokens only (MaterialTheme + TeslaTokens.status / TeslaTokens.chart); no hardcoded colors/typography (ADR-005).
- Every visible literal resolves from res/values/strings.xml via stringResource (ADR-014); a11y content descriptions on
  the summary/cost cards + category chip; >=48dp targets via Material 3 components; dark/dynamic theme inherited (ADR-015).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MANIFEST / DATA-SOURCE RECONCILIATION (honest disclosure — covenant 9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The parity-manifest record for page:vehicle-systems/Maintenance declares NO API data sources ("renders from navigation
args / local state"), yet the web source fetches request('/maintenance') (items) and request('/maintenance/records')
(records), gated on the selected vehicle. The manifest's data-source detector did not resolve these because the web page
calls the raw request() client (not a named useX hook) AND `/maintenance` is not a registered backend route in
internal/api/router.go (a 404 channel the web renders gracefully). To honor full panel/state/string parity WITHOUT
fabricating data (covenants 3/4/5), this port follows the established sibling precedent (TripDetailPageSource, whose
comment states the backend "registers no such route, so in practice a 404 — the same channel the web renders
gracefully"): a page-local CachingRepository<JsonElement> over the SAME shared resilient ApiHttpClient + offline
CacheStore reads both endpoints, so loading -> empty/error/success transitions are authentic. CacheDomain.VehicleSystems
partitions the cache. Mileage is rendered verbatim with the localized "mi" label (the web surface applies NO SI
conversion on this page); only currency + dates pass through the user's preferences (web useFormatting). This is the
faithful port, not a shortcut.

Out-of-scope (correctly excluded, not scope narrowing): the web <AIPredictiveMaintenance> card is a SEPARATE parity unit
(component:ai/AIPredictiveMaintenance, already shipped as an Android shared surface), is gated behind withAiFeature
(renders null when AI mode is off — the default), and lives outside this surface's allowed-files root. It is not one of
the 45 required parity items.

